"No god or power chose Nala; she came by accident, not for a purpose."
"This season the boundary around the world thins in places, as the northern cult presses on it."
"Where a leyline runs under a thinning, a sleeping soul can slip through from beyond."
"Alan's soul, asleep, slipped through above the leyline under Moss Hollow on a near-full moon."
"The System built her body at the hollow from her soul rather than from the body she left."
"Her clothes came whole because they were worn close at the crossing, and the System took them as hers."
"The System reads Nala as a plain Tier 0 human; Identify shows nothing strange."
"Heritage sense finds no lineage in Nala at all, which puzzles anyone who has it."
"A soul from past the boundary reads as a faint cold draught to mana sight, felt only up close."
"The northern cult would take a soul from beyond as a door for their Lords, and hunt her."
"The churches of the Stars would call a soul from beyond a wonder, and want to keep her."
"Nala's Language Seed covers the common tongue and script, but not Old Breinish or other tongues."
"Nala's Class, when it comes, grows from what she does most with steady intent."
"Nothing brings Nala home; the way she came does not open back."
